<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Momentum Radar — fastest-growing token launches</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css">
</head>
<body>
<header class="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">MOMENTUM RADAR &middot; MOMENTUM-1</p>
    <h1>Ride the fastest-growing launches before the crowd</h1>
    <p class="sub" id="meta">Loading the sealed snapshot&hellip;</p>
  </div>
</header>

<main class="wrap">
  <section class="movers" aria-label="Hottest movers">
    <h2>Hottest movers <span class="muted">fastest 7-day TVL growth on the board</span></h2>
    <div class="mover-grid" id="movers"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="controls" aria-label="Board controls">
    <label>Search <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Protocol name or slug" autocomplete="off"></label>
    <label>Category <select id="cat"><option value="">All categories</option></select></label>
    <label>Chain <select id="chain"><option value="">All chains</option></select></label>
    <label>Sort <select id="sort">
      <option value="rank">Rank</option>
      <option value="implied">Implied value</option>
      <option value="growth">7-day growth</option>
      <option value="tvl">TVL</option>
      <option value="age">Age</option>
      <option value="name">Name A&ndash;Z</option>
    </select></label>
    <label class="check"><input id="watch" type="checkbox"> Watchlist only</label>
    <label class="check"><input id="hot" type="checkbox"> Hot only (7d &gt; 0%)</label>
  </section>

  <p class="count" id="count"></p>

  <section class="panel">
    <table id="board">
      <thead><tr>
        <th data-k="rank">#</th><th data-k="name">Protocol</th><th data-k="category">Category</th>
        <th data-k="tvl">TVL</th><th data-k="growth">7d growth</th>
        <th data-k="momentum">Momentum</th><th data-k="implied">Implied value</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody id="rows"></tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="panel detail" id="detail" hidden>
    <div class="detail-head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker" id="d-rank"></p>
        <h2 id="d-name"></h2>
        <p class="muted" id="d-sub"></p>
      </div>
      <p class="big" id="d-value"></p>
    </div>
    <h3>How the value is built</h3>
    <table class="model" id="d-model"></table>
    <h3>Farm plan &mdash; timed to the momentum</h3>
    <ol class="steps" id="d-steps"></ol>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>Already trading &mdash; the market&rsquo;s own values</h2>
    <p class="muted">These protocols already have a token, so the board shows what the market pays for them, not a model. They set the ratios the pre-token board is priced from.</p>
    <table id="live">
      <thead><tr><th>Protocol</th><th>Category</th><th>TVL</th><th>Market cap</th><th>7d</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="live-rows"></tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>How the momentum model works</h2>
    <p>Every protocol in the snapshot that records no token is priced from the snapshot&rsquo;s own figures. The category&rsquo;s ratio is the median market-cap-to-TVL of the protocols in that category that already trade, shrunk toward the whole snapshot&rsquo;s median when the category has few live peers. Base value is TVL times that ratio. Then growth does the ranking, and it compounds: the seven-day TVL change, clamped to &minus;40%..+100%, is raised to the third power, so +18% in a week is worth 1.64x, +100% is worth 8x and &minus;20% is worth 0.51x. A week of +10% or better earns a hot bonus of 1.15x, and a protocol under a year old with no token earns a fresh bonus of 1.10x. Running on more chains adds 5% a chain, up to four extra chains. Last, a size adjustment discounts the giants and lifts the small: the value is multiplied by the square root of $100M over TVL, clamped to 0.25x..2.5x, so the board ranks where the money is moving per dollar already there, not where it already sits. Without it the same giants would hold the top ten whatever they grew, and this would be a size table in a different colour. Nothing here is a prediction that a token launches, or when: the implied value is this entry&rsquo;s own claim about what a launch would be worth if the money kept moving the way it moved this week.</p>
    <p class="muted">Watchlist: the 40 protocols at or above $50,000,000 of TVL that record no token and are not a wrapped, staked or bridged product of one that trades. The board carries all 40, plus every other pre-token protocol the same rule keeps, at any TVL.</p>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="wrap muted">Implied values are this entry&rsquo;s own claim, never a prediction of a launch. Data: the sealed DefiLlama snapshot.</footer>

<script src="../data.js"></script>
<script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
